.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt PFCTL 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pfctl
.Nd parse, print and verify pf.conf rulesets and table files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl D Ar name=value
.Op Fl t Ar table Op Fl T Ar command Op Fl f Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the front-end of the FreeBSD pfctl tool port.
It parses the supported pf.conf subset, prints the compact normalized form produced by
.Dq pfctl -nv ,
and parses table files.
This build has no pf ABI yet, so every mutating action is refused and
.Fl n
is required; the ruleset is never loaded.
.Pp
The supported syntax, the canonical output form and the documented
divergences are described in
.Pa docs/pfctl.md .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n
Dry run: parse and validate only.
Required until the pf ABI lands.
.It Fl v
Print the normalized configuration (or table) to standard output.
.It Fl f Ar file
Read the configuration (or table file with
.Fl T )
from
.Ar file .
.It Fl D Ar name=value
Define a macro before parsing.
Repeatable.
.It Fl t Ar table
Select the table for
.Fl T .
.It Fl T Ar command
Table command:
.Cm add ,
.Cm delete ,
.Cm replace
or
.Cm test .
.Cm show
and
.Cm flush
need the pf ABI.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A parse, validation or usage error prints a line-numbered message
.Pq file:line: message
and exits 1.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tcpdump 1 ,
.Xr pf.conf 5
